# Thumbnails of the main menu: NAME X Y SCALE. The window of 174/SCALE PMD 85 pixels with the top left corner at X,Y
# (of the 288x256 screen) is magnified SCALE times (3 = 58x58 pixels, 2 = 87x87, 1 = 174x174), the pixels stay sharp.
# Optional operations on the 288x256 screen before the crop: WxH+X+Y>X2,Y2 copies a rectangle to X2,Y2, -WxH+X+Y erases it,
# =WxH+X+Y keeps it (everything outside the kept rectangles is erased). The erases go first, then the copies, then the keeps.
# make-thumbs.sh makes <NAME>.png (174x174, 1 bit) of <NAME>.bmp, a screenshot of the game (PMD_SCREENSHOT).
